scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: hogans-heroes
run_id: 4
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the from_file_or_default unwrap_or_default pattern that
    swallows parse/permission errors. Config tests exist but none distinguish NotFound
    from other error types.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: Reviewer flagged CWE-209 on ServerError Display/Debug, noting Debug impl
    exposes inner string. TEA also wrote security tests at security.rs:62-72 for internal
    detail leakage. However, the Io(transparent) variant forwarding raw OS errors
    was not specifically called out.
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-113 header injection tests requiring tenant ID with CRLF/null
    bytes to be rejected. Dev implemented HeaderValue::from_str() validation. Reviewer
    verified it. However, the type-safety recommendation (use TenantId from axiathon-core
    instead of raw String) was not flagged by any phase.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer checked dependencies but focused on unused keyring
    dep and toml version mismatch, not the workspace inheritance pattern.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer explicitly flagged as [HIGH]: ''RawConfig silently ignores unknown
    fields... #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] should be used with an explicit allowlist,
    or at minimum unknown fields should produce a warning.'' Directly matches the
    finding about token field being silently ignored.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...)). The config_loading tests were written by TEA and passed in dev, but
    the logical tautology was not flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase identified the zero-assertion test using ''let _ = config''.
    Despite 12 config_loading tests and SOUL.md principle #4 about vacuously true
    tests, this test quality issue was missed.'
